Docker engine "Ubuntu 24.04 LTS" (laptop): the run relay listens on 172.17.0.1 and a run's proxy reaches it at host-gateway (checked with a probe container).
Checking the connection to the organisation, as `wardyn-runnerd doctor` does:
skip  trusted-ca   no extra CA bundle is set: the system roots only
ok    org-url      ORG (from --org)
ok    dns          127.0.0.1 is an address: nothing to resolve
ok    proxy        direct (no proxy applies to this address)
skip  tls          plain http://: there is no handshake to check
ok    healthz      status ok, server version 0.10.0
ok    wire         the runner stream route switched to a WebSocket: the upgrade gets through
skip  service      no service is installed for this runner: it runs only where you start `wardyn-runnerd serve`, and `wardyn-runnerd setup` installs one
skip  status       the service has not run yet: there is no status.json in ROOT/home/.config/wardyn/runner
The wardyn CLI now points at ORG (change it with wardyn login <url>).
Registering this computer. At a terminal it asks for the runner's limits (Enter takes each suggestion); otherwise it registers with the limits it suggests.
